.TH "REPORTINGOBSERVER.REPORTINGOBSERVER" "3JS" "April 21, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
ReportingObserver.ReportingObserver \- ReportingObserver:
ReportingObserver() constructor
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]ReportingObserver()\f[B]\f[R] constructor of the
Reporting API creates a new \f[CR]ReportingObserver\f[R] object
instance, which can be used to collect and access reports.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
new ReportingObserver(callback)
new ReportingObserver(callback, options)
.EE
.SS Parameters
.TP
\f[B]callback\f[R]
A callback function that runs when the observer starts to collect
reports (i.e., via \f[CR]ReportingObserver.observe()\f[R]).
The callback function is given two parameters:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]reports\f[R]
A sequence of objects representing the reports collected in the
observer\(cqs report queue.
.RS
.PP
Report objects are expected to have the following properties:
.TP
\f[B]body\f[R]
An object representing the body of the report.
The structure of the report (in particular of its body), depends on its
\f[CR]type\f[R].
.TP
\f[B]type\f[R]
A string indicating the type of the report.
For information on report types see \f[CR]options.types\f[R] below.
.TP
\f[B]url\f[R]
A string representing the URL of the document that generated the report.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]observer\f[R]
A reference to the same \f[CR]ReportingObserver\f[R] object, allowing
for recursive report collection, and so on.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]options\f[R] \f[I](optional)\f[R]
An object allowing you to set the options for creating the object.
The available options are:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]types\f[R]
An array of strings representing the types of report to be collected by
this observer.
Available types include:
.RS
.TP
\f[B]coep\f[R]
Violations of the site\(cqs \f[CR]Cross\-Origin\-Embedder\-Policy\f[R]
(COEP).
Reports are \f[CR]COEPViolationReport\f[R] instances.
.TP
\f[B]coop\f[R]
Violations of the site\(cqs \f[CR]Cross\-Origin\-Opener\-Policy\f[R]
(COOP).
Reports are \f[CR]COOPViolationReport\f[R] instances.
.TP
\f[B]crash\f[R]
Browser crash reports.
Reports are \f[CR]CrashReport\f[R] instances.
Note that crash reports aren\(cqt retrievable via a
\f[CR]ReportingObserver\f[R] but can be sent to a server.
.TP
\f[B]csp\-violation\f[R]
Violations of the site\(cqs CSP policy.
Reports are \f[CR]CSPViolationReport\f[R] instances.
.TP
\f[B]deprecation\f[R]
Deprecated features used by the site.
Reports are \f[CR]DeprecationReport\f[R] instances.
.TP
\f[B]integrity\-violation\f[R]
Violations of the page\(cqs integrity policy.
Reports are \f[CR]IntegrityViolationReport\f[R] instances.
.TP
\f[B]intervention\f[R]
Features blocked by the user agent, for example, if an ad significantly
impacts page performance.
Reports are \f[CR]InterventionReport\f[R] instances.
.TP
\f[B]permissions\-policy\-violation\f[R]
Violations of the site\(cqs \f[CR]Permissions\-Policy\f[R].
Reports are \f[CR]PermissionsPolicyViolationReport\f[R] instances.
If this option is omitted, all supported types are collected.
.RE
.TP
\f[B]buffered\f[R]
A boolean that defines whether the reports that were generated before
the observer was able to be created should be observable
(\f[CR]true\f[R]) or not (\f[CR]false\f[R]).
.RE
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Display specific report types
This code shows how to create a \f[CR]ReportingObserver\f[R] that could
be used to observe \f[CR]deprecation\f[R] and
\f[CR]integrity\-violation\f[R] reports.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] options = {
  types: [\(dqdeprecation\(dq, \(dqintegrity\-violation\(dq],
  buffered: \f[B]true\f[R],
};

\f[B]const\f[R] observer = \f[B]new\f[R] ReportingObserver((reports, observer) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  reportBtn.onclick = () \f[B]=>\f[R] displayReports(reports);
}, options);
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.IP \(bu 2
Reporting API
